Bash	cd <work>; grep -rn "apply_coupon\|discount_percent\|sign_up" . --exclude-dir=.git; python3 -c "; from api.routes import handle; print(handle('/coupon', {'coupon':'NOPE'}))"; D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/filing.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md; ls $D/scripts
Bash	cd <work>; D=<craft>/skills/github; gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; gh label list; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh filing billing/tax.py accounts/signup.py vat sign_up email VAT 2>&1 | tail -5
text	Checking the tracker for existing issues before I file two of the findings.
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.LuvNpl
Bash	cd <work>; T=$(mktemp -d); cat > $T/a.md <<'EOF'; `billing/tax.py:4`: the docstring of `vat` says "Returns the VAT on amount, in cents." The function returns euros: a `Decimal` quantized to `0.01`. Its only caller, `get_invoice_total` in `billing/invoice.py:5`, adds the result to an order total in euros.; ; A reader who trusts the docstring can divide the result by 100, or multiply a caller's value by 100, and get a wrong invoice total.; ; Fix: say "in euros, rounded to the cent" in the docstring.; ; Out of scope for #14 Order total is off by a cent on some orders: that fix changes `orders/`, and this is in `billing/`.; EOF; cat > $T/b.md <<'EOF'; `accounts/signup.py:4`: `sign_up` checks and stores the email exactly as typed. So `Bob@shop.test` and `bob@shop.test` sign up as two accounts for the same mailbox.; ; Steps:; ; ```python; from accounts.signup import sign_up; sign_up("bob@shop.test", "h1"); sign_up("Bob@shop.test", "h2")  # no ValueError: a second account; ```; ; Expected: the second call raises `ValueError("this email has an account")`.; ; A likely fix compares and stores a normalized email (for example `email.strip().lower()`). Which normalization to use is a product decision: the local part of an address is case-sensitive by the standard, though almost no provider treats it so. The login lookup must use the same normalization.; ; Out of scope for #14 Order total is off by a cent on some orders: that fix changes `orders/`, and this is in `accounts/`.; EOF; gh issue create --repo acme/shop --title "The docstring of vat says cents, but it returns euros" --label documentation --body-file $T/a.md; gh issue create --repo acme/shop --title "Sign-up treats emails that differ only in case as two accounts" --label bug --body-file $T/b.md
Bash	cd <work>; python3 -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -3; git status --short
Bash	cd <work>; rm -rf api/__pycache__ billing/__pycache__; git status --short
text	I checked each finding against the code and filed issues for two of them. I changed no code, and the branch and PR are as you left them. All four findings are outside `orders/`, the module the #14 fix changed, so none of them could go into this change.  | # | Finding | Result | |---|---|---| | 1 | `get_invoice_total` name | **Not filed.** It is only a naming preference, and no project rule asks for it. You can file it if you want it. | | 2 | `vat` docstring says cents | **Filed as #17 The docstring of vat says cents, but it returns euros** (label `documentation`). The finding is correct: the function returns euros rounded to the cent. I filed it because a docstring that says something false is worth an issue. | | 3 | `sign_up` treats emails that differ in case as different | **Filed as #18 Sign-up treats emails that differ only in case as two accounts** (label `bug`). The issue includes steps to reproduce it. It also says that how to normalize the email is a product decision, and that the login lookup must use the same rule. | | 4 | `discount_percent` KeyError gives a 500 | **Declined.** This error cannot happen through the API. `CouponRequest` in `api/schemas.py:6` rejects an unknown code before `discount_percent` runs. `/coupon` is the only way to reach that function. I called `handle('/coupon', {'coupon': 'NOPE'})` and got a 400 "unknown coupon code", not a 500. |  There were no existing issues on these files, so nothing was a duplicate. Note that acme/shop is a public repository, so the two new issues are public.  The project's test command, `python -m pytest`, did not run: pytest is not installed here. Because I changed no code, this has no effect on the branch. My check of finding 4 left `__pycache__` folders in the tree, and I deleted them, so the tree is clean.
